  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-x+4 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+2x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-{x}^{2}-2x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x+8}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2$ by the linear binomial $x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3{x}^{2}-x+4,$ and\n\n- the remainder $-6.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2}{x+2}=3{x}^{2}-x+4-\\frac{6}{x+2}.\n$$",
